<h1>Rotate and Translate</h1>
<hr align="left" width="100.526%" size="5" class="whs3">
<p><span lang="EN-GB">This command is accessible from the</span> <span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Registration &gt; Rotate and Translate</b></span>.</p>
<p class="description"><span lang="EN-GB" class="Command" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> <span class="Command">Rotate and Translate</span> <span lang="EN-GB">command offers possibility for manual adjustment of entity position. The command works with whole entities - no matter if these are entirely or partially selected.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">Select an entity or part of it and call</span> <span class="Command">Rotate and Translate</span><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>.</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">The following dialog will appear:</span></p>
<p><img src="Images/rotate_and_translate.gif" width="220px" height="515px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt=""></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Reference</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription">I<span lang="EN-GB">t is used for defining the rotation and translation axis:</span></p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB"><b style="font-weight:bold;">World</b> – the axes of the global co-ordinate system.</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB"><b style="font-weight:bold;">Viewport</b> – the axes of the viewport.</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="Note" id="p3"><span lang="EN-GB"><b style="font-weight:bold;">Note:</b> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:normal;">If there is an active alignment in the document, the axes of the global co-ordinate system will coincide with the axes of the active alignment (world reference).</span></span></p>
<p class="sub-head">Rotate group:</p>
<p class="parameterstitle">Centre</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">It is used for defining the centre of rotation:</p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Selection extents' centre</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">– this is the point, which is located in the middle of entity’s extents.</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB"><b style="font-weight:bold;">Centre view</b> – this is the point, which is located in the centre of view.</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB"><b style="font-weight:bold;">Point (pick point)</b> – when you pick a point, KUBE gets the closest datum point or vertex to the place you picked to.</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB"><b style="font-weight:bold;">Datum point</b> – select a datum point from the drop-down list.</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB"><b style="font-weight:bold;">Line (pick two points)</b> – when you pick two points, KUBE gets the closest datum points or vertices to the places you picked to and defines a rotation axis. In this case all sliders work in the same way – the rotation is around the defined line.</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB"><b style="font-weight:bold;">Datum line</b> – select a datum line from the drop-down list. In this case all sliders work in the same way – the rotation is around the selected line.</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB"><b style="font-weight:bold;">Origin</b> – this is the point, which is in the origin of the co-ordinate system (with co-ordinates 0, 0, 0).</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="Note" id="p2"><span lang="EN-GB"><b style="font-weight:bold;">Note:</b> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:normal;">If there is an active alignment in the document, the axes of the origin co-ordinate system will coincide with the axes of the active alignment (origin reference).</span></span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle">Datums</p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span style="font-weight:normal;">Select an existing datum point or line when 'Datum point' or 'Datum Line' is selected for</span> Centre<span style="font-weight:normal;">. Otherwise inactive.</span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Around</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription">The three axes <b>OX</b>, <b>OY</b>, or <b>OZ <span style="font-weight:normal;">belong</span></b> to the current co-ordinate system. Select one of them to set it as axis of rotation.</p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><b style="font-weight:bold;"><span lang="EN-GB">Angle</span></b></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-GB">Enter an angle step in degrees and using the</span> <span class="Button">Apply</span> <span lang="EN-GB">button rotate the selected entity.</span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Manual rotation</b></span> slider</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Move the slider to rotate at the selected centre and axis.</p>
<p class="sub-head">Translate group:</p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><b><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Along</b></span></b></p>
<p class="parameterdescription">The three axes <b>OX</b>, <b>OY</b>, or <b>OZ <span style="font-weight:normal;">belong</span></b> to the current co-ordinate system. Select one of them to set it as axis for translation.</p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><b style="font-weight:bold;"><span lang="EN-GB">Offset</span></b></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-GB">Enter an offset step in mm and use the</span> <span class="Button">Apply</span> <span lang="EN-GB">button to translate the selection.</span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Manual translation</b></span> slider</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Move the slider to translate at the selected axis.</p>
<p class="sub-head">Slider sensitivity group:</p>
<p class="bullet">It is used only when user rotates/translates entity by the sliders. It allows three levels of sensitivity (<b>Coarse</b>, <b>Medium</b>, and <b>Fine</b>).</p>
<p class="sub-head">Home position group:</p>
<p class="bullet">When you are satisfied with a position, you can save it as a start point for further fittings. Such position is called home position.</p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-GB"><b style="font-weight:bold;">Set</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-GB">Sets a new home position;</span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-GB"><b style="font-weight:bold;">Go to</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-GB">Discards any rotations and translations and returns the entity in its home position.</span></p>
